Z||000000||Pyric||11-19-2001||09:45 AM||||The dash in my GT is starting to show scrub marks where the grey paint has rubbed off.  Does anyone know where I can get some interior paint?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Pheagey||11-19-2001||10:17 AM||||I also haev an interest in interior paint (gray is so drab looking)<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ambush||11-19-2001||10:46 AM||||DO NOT DO IT!!! stay away from it if you can. It scratches very easily. I wont even mention the smell it leaves in your car when you put your dash back in. Go to your local fabric store and buy some vinyl or something like that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||NEO Cesek Racing||11-19-2001||02:09 PM||||talk to FieroMaster, he repainted his interior black. it came out really well but i can't remember which kind of paint he said he used.  he's supposed to repaint mine with me when i scrounge up the money. i didn't notice a smell in his at all. i suppose it depends on what kind of paint you get. <BR>he also took all the vinyl out of the car when he painted it. it only took one guy with a screw driver 4 hours from start to finish.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pyric||11-19-2001||02:16 PM||||Well, I know it was painted at the factory, because if you buy replacement pieces, they are that hideous brown/orange color (which is the color the scrub marks are).  I was pretty sure there is a special paint for the interior that is available.  <P>Maybe I'll try the dealer...||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||11-19-2001||04:08 PM||||any auto paint supply store has vinyl colors. But if you just want it black, you can buy that at any auto parts store. Main thing is to make sure its absolutely clean of any wax, polish, or even fingerprints. Use a brush and solvent (alcohol, thinner). Paint it in very light coats, until its covered. Ive had no problem with scratching or peeling, mines been done at least 3 years. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||NEPTUNE||11-19-2001||04:15 PM||||Discount auto parts has it, as do most auto parts stores. I wouldn't recommend a drastic color change, but if you just want to make old stuff look new, it works pretty well. I have used it on a dark blue Ford and a red Nissan with excellent results. Make sure the surface is clean and maybe scuff it with steel wool first.||||reg||6
Z||000007||Loki||11-19-2001||04:41 PM||||Got vinyl pain from wal-mart...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroloki.com/DASH.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroloki.com/Rearconsole.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroloki.com/centerconsole.jpg"> <P>Just make sure you cean the hell outt the surface first......The a few coats and its done...<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">  <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000008||88extinct||11-19-2001||07:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>The dash in my GT is starting to show scrub marks where the grey paint has rubbed off.  Does anyone know where I can get some interior paint?  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I did some repainting on my 88 med beige.  Used a Dupont Vinyl paint.  The store mixed it and you put it in a Preval spray bottle.  The paint code for the med beige is 66BN/9098.  Hope that helps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||tgowens||11-19-2001||09:48 PM||||I repaint interior pieces all the time - I use SEM paint for the color match to the original and I have an '97GT that I did the interior in black with Vinyl spray......<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
